"Symmetric edge polytopes are not gamma-positive (https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.02424)\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Title: Symmetric edge polytopes are not gamma-positive ... A conjecture posed by Ohsugi and Tsuchiya (2019) postulates that the Ehrhart $h^*$-polynomials of symmetric edge polytopes are $γ$-positive.\nTitle: Symmetric edge polytopes are not gamma-positive\nAuthors: Luis Ferroni\nDate: Thu Jul  2 16:52:48 2026\n\nA conjecture posed by Ohsugi and Tsuchiya (2019) postulates that the Ehrhart $h^*$-polynomials of symmetric edge polytopes are $γ$-positive. We disprove this conjecture by exhibiting an infinite family of counterexamples. The smallest example provided by our construction is a $36$-dimensional symmetric edge polytope.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLinks among Finite Geometries, (https://doktori.bibl.u-szeged.hu/628/1/diszRJ.pdf)\nciteturn1search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Wilson [47] identified the following four families (a)–(d) of edge-transitive ... The main goal of this chapter is to confirm this conjecture by proving ... graphs \\(R_n(a,r)\\)Let $\\Gamma$ be the rose window graph $R_n(a,r)$.\nWilson [47] identified the following four families (a)–(d) of edge-transitive\nrose window graphs \\(R_n(a,r)\\) given below and conjectured that these graphs\nexhaust the whole class of edge-transitive rose window graphs. The conjec-\nture was confirmed by Kovács, Kutnar and Marušič [33].(a) \\(R_n(2,1);\\)  \n(b) \\(R_{2m}(m-2,m-1);\\)  \n(c) \\(R_{12m}(3m+2,3m-1)\\) and \\(R_{12m}(3m-2,3m+1);\\)  \n(d) \\(R_{2m}(2b,r),\\) where \\(b^2\\equiv\\pm1\\pmod m,\\ 2\\le 2b\\le m,\\) and \\(r\\in\\{1,m-1\\}\\) is odd.Observe that family (a) is contained in family (d) and that each graph\n\\(R_n(a,r)\\) in families (a)-(d) satisfies the condition \\(1 \\le a,r \\le n/2\\). The\nlatter is is a natural restriction by the following easy observations (see also\n[